1059:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) There are two mode of transfer:
1060:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Blocking mode: The communication is performed in polling mode.
1061:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart.c ****            The HAL status of all data processing is returned by the same function
1062:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart.c ****            after finishing transfer.
1063:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Non-Blocking mode: The communication is performed using Interrupts
1064:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart.c ****            or DMA, These API's return the HAL status.
1065:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart.c ****            The end of the data processing will be indicated through the
1066:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart.c ****            dedicated UART IRQ when using Interrupt mode or the DMA IRQ when
1067:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart.c ****            using DMA mode.
1068:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart.c ****            The HAL_UART_TxCpltCallback(), HAL_UART_RxCpltCallback() user callbacks
1069:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart.c ****            will be executed respectively at the end of the transmit or Receive process
1070:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart.c ****            The HAL_UART_ErrorCallback()user callback will be executed when a communication error is
1071:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart.c **** 
